<title>TURKEY: Turkish Bossa Q1 profit turns to loss.</title>
<headline>Turkish Bossa Q1 profit turns to loss.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-March 1997 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share loss   (lira)    30.05   vs   240.86 profit</p>
<p>    Loss			    135.23   vs   433.55 profit</p>
<p>    Net sales		   6,596.09   vs 3,997.19</p>
<p>    Operating profit	    612.62   vs   980.26</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	  528.46   vs   293.08</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense	 226.43   vs   296.19</p>
<p>    Interest paid		 680.44   vs   329.07</p>
<p>    Total debts		12,652.91   vs 7,584.12</p>
<p>    Equity			8,337.69   vs 4,678.80</p>
<p>    Capital		     4,500.00   vs 1,800.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Bossa Ticaret ve Sanayi Isletmeleri T.A.S. is a leading textile company largely owned by Turkish Sabanc conglomerate.</p>
<p>The company will pay a 270 lira cash dividend per 1,000 lira nominal-valued share from 196 profits and issue 1.5 bonuses for each existing share from May 28 for the capital increase from 1.8 trillion lira to 4.5 trillion.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 77 percent annual wholesale inflation in March.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875.</p>
</text>
